}
<style is:global>
  valstara-signup-form [hidden] {
    display: none !important;
  }
  /* While the bar shows, the page reserves its height below the content,
     and a focused element lands at least 16px clear of it (E11.5-11h). */
  html[data-signup-dock='visible'] {
    scroll-padding-block-end: calc(var(--signup-dock-height) + var(--space-2));
  }

  html[data-signup-dock='visible'] body {
    padding-block-end: var(--signup-dock-height);
  }

  valstara-signup-form {
    display: block;
  }

  /*
    `:not([hidden])` so an author `display` never wins over the `hidden`
    attribute: author rules beat the UA `[hidden] { display: none }` by origin,
    so a bare `form { display: grid }` would keep a `form.hidden = true` form
    visible. The island hides the form this way once a signup succeeds.
  */
  /*
    The hero form card from the final design (Hero.dc.html, E11.5-11l), on
    the E11.5-11c form. A surface card, radius 12, --shadow-1 plus the
    dark-only edge, 20px padding (24px from 48rem). Small: the field, then a
    full-width button 12px below it. From 48rem the field and the button share
    one row, 8px apart, and a field error sits under the field only. The
    Field's wrapper steps aside (display: contents) so its label and hint span
    the row above. Under the row: the microline 12px below, the Turnstile slot
    12px below that only while Cloudflare shows the widget, a 1px --line
    divider 20px below, the trust facts 16px under the divider and the
    marketing box 16px below them. Rows that hold only hidden elements
    collapse to nothing.
